The degradation comes from a single fault: the `profile` service is crash-looping, so it is effectively unavailable. Its pod restarted 3–6 times with container readiness at 0 for the whole incident. Kubelet events show the container cycling through Failed, Killed and BackOff. The profile server spans disappear entirely during the incident.

The effect reaches users through `frontend`. Every `profile.Profile/GetProfiles` call from frontend errors almost instantly. As a result, `/hotels` (660 requests) and `/recommendations` (357 requests) return HTTP 500 to users, and frontend logs 1140 "Get profiles failed" errors.

I did not find a separate fault in the other services. Reservation, rate and search show only small latency increases with no errors, and their container CPU, memory and restart metrics are flat. I also did not find network-level metrics for these connections. The telemetry does not show why the profile container crashes, so the fault kind rests on the restart and readiness pattern.
